@copilot Update this existing PR directly by adding the missing span-status assertion to JmsCamelTest.faultedCamelProcessCountsDeliveredMessage in instrumentation/camel-2.20/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/camel/v2_20/JmsCamelTest.java.

The fault-only route already calls exchange.getOut().setFault(true), exercising request.getExchange().isFailed() without throwing an exception. The test currently asserts error.type="_OTHER" on the process faultQueue span and messaging metrics, but does not assert that the span status is ERROR. Extend that same process-span assertion to verify StatusData.error() using the repository's OpenTelemetry span assertion API, with the necessary imports. Preserve the existing error.type and metric assertions.

Keep the production change and all other existing tests unchanged. This is a small addition to the existing real-Camel integration test, not a request for more scenarios, a new harness, or broader coverage. Follow repository instructions, format the changed file with the narrowest spotlessApply task, and run the relevant existing JmsCamelTest integration test. Preserve this PR's current draft/ready state and base branch. Do not create a separate or follow-up PR, request a review, or add unrelated changes.

